DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     Prometheus is a monitoring system that gathers metrics from its targets
     by fetching them through HTTP GET requests.  Metrics are identified by a
     name and an optional set of labels.  Sample values are required to be nu‐
     merical.

     The pprroommeetthheeuuss__ssyyssccttll__eexxppoorrtteerr utility prints the values of sysctl nodes
     to standard output, formatted such that they can be scraped by Prometheus
     directly.  By default, it prints metrics for all numerically repre‐
     sentable nodes in the sysctl namespace.  It is also possible to limit
     output to a smaller number of metrics by specifying one or more prefixes
     as arguments.

     Metrics printed by this utility are named ‘sysctl_’, followed by the name
     of the sysctl node having its ‘.’ separators replaced by ‘_’.  Components
     on which it is desirable to aggregate (e.g., names of devices) are omit‐
     ted from the metric's name, but are appended as labels instead.

     There are two different methods for exporting the output of
     pprroommeetthheeuuss__ssyyssccttll__eexxppoorrtteerr to Prometheus.  The first method is to period‐
     ically invoke this utility through cron(8) and store its output in a
     textfile.  The metrics in this textfile can then be served over HTTP us‐
     ing the Prometheus node exporter's textfile collector.  The second method
     is to run this utility through inetd(8).  TCP port 9124 has been allo‐
     cated for this purpose.

     The following options are available:

     --dd      Print descriptions of metrics when available.

     --ee _p_a_t_t_e_r_n
             Same as --ii, except exclude metrics that match _p_a_t_t_e_r_n.

     --gg      Gzip compresses the HTTP response body.

     --hh      Precede the output with a HTTP response header.  This flag is re‐
             quired when running this utility through inetd(8).

     --ii _p_a_t_t_e_r_n
             If specified, include metrics that match _p_a_t_t_e_r_n.  The format of
             _p_a_t_t_e_r_n is to be a regular expression as described in
             re_format(7).  The provided regular expression is tested against
             the Prometheus metric name.

